---
/**
 * Open Source Projects page
 * A curated selection of what is worth looking at, not a list of everything that exists.
 */
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro'
import ProjectCategorySection from '../components/projects/ProjectCategorySection.astro'
import Section from '../components/site/Section.astro'
import { categories, projects } from '../data/projects'
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'
import { generateSeoMetadata } from '../utils/seo-metadata'

// SEO metadata (kept neutral, non-promotional)
const seo = generateSeoMetadata({
  title: 'Projects',
  description:
    'A selection of the open source work I\'ve done: VS Code extensions, a Debian-based distribution, PHP and Moodle tooling, and Windows repair scripts.',
  keywords:
    'open source, developer tools, vscode extensions, debian, linux, php, moodle, codeigniter, tooling',
})
---

<Layout title={seo.title} description={seo.description} keywords={seo.keywords}>
  <div
    class="content-visibility-auto container mx-auto px-4 pt-20"
    style="contain-intrinsic-size: 500px"
  >
    <!-- Hero -->
    <Hero
      title="Things I've Built and Kept Around"
      description="A selection, not an inventory. Some of these are recent, some are from years ago and archived, some are very small. They're here because each one says something about what I've worked on."
    />

    <!-- Context / framing -->
    <Section>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-zinc-300">
        <p>
          Most of these exist because something was broken, repetitive, or frustrating, and I needed
          a way to deal with it. None of them were built as products or startups.
        </p>

        <p>
          They're grouped by the kind of work they came out of rather than by how new or popular
          they are. A few are archived and I've left them here anyway - they're the clearest record
          I have of where I came from.
        </p>

        <p>
          I don't maintain everything at the same pace, and I don't offer guaranteed support or
          timelines. Pauses and limited capacity are part of keeping this sustainable.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <!-- Curated projects, grouped by maturity -->
    {
      categories.map((category) => (
        <ProjectCategorySection category={category} projects={projects} />
      ))
    }

    <!-- Everything else -->
    <Section>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-zinc-300">
        <p>
          Plenty is missing on purpose. There are around fifty VS Code extensions published over
          the years - more snippets, extension packs, generators for other stacks - along with
          older utilities and experiments. They're all still there, they just don't each need a
          paragraph.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/ManuelGil"
            class="text-primary transition-colors hover:text-primary-dark"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            The rest of it lives on GitHub →
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </Section>
  </div>
</Layout>
